      "writtenOn": "2017-09-05T04:38:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a very common case where this does not happen: IPv6-only networks with a NAT64, such as the IMS PDN on many carriers. On such networks we remain in STARTING until the network disconnects and never get a link state up notification.\n\nCan we add a testcase for this as well? Based on my reading of the current patchset, in that case I believe we won\u0027t unregister the observer. Regardless of whether my reading is correct or not, a test is better.\n\nDon\u0027t remove this test, of course - it tests a harder-to-reproduce and thus harder-to-get right case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 185,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 31
      },
